#### 14.5.11 Spec-Compliant Percentage Resolution
Refactor percentage resolution to follow CSS Values Level 4 §5.1.1:
"The computed value of a percentage is the specified percentage value. Resolution is deferred to layout."
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-values-4/#percentages

Current state: Percentage resolvers try to resolve during cascade, but boxes don't exist yet.
Wrong approach: Adding null checks and deferring resolution with CssValue.Null hacks.
Correct approach: Percentages should NOT resolve during cascade at all.

**Legitimate bug fixes to KEEP:**
- [x] Fix Tree.Get_Next_Sibling() bounds check (index + 1 < Count, not index < Count)
- [x] Fix Find_Containing_Block() TreeWalker bug (was using Target as root, parentNode() always returned null)
- [x] Fix Resolve_Vertical() AUTO height check (can't call AsDecimal on AUTO)
- [x] Fix percentage normalization (0-100 range to 0-1 range when resolving)

**Workarounds to REVERT:**
- [ ] Remove null check hack in Containing_Block_Logical_Width() - should throw if box is null
- [ ] Remove null check hack in Containing_Block_Logical_Height() - should throw if box is null
- [ ] Remove CssValue.Null deferral in Derive_ComputedValue
- [ ] Remove manual percentage resolution in Resolve_Horizontal()
- [ ] Remove UpdateContentWidth() from CssPrincipalBox
- [ ] Remove ResolveWidthsTopDown() test fixture hack (replaced with ForceFullLayout)

**Spec-compliant implementation:**
- [ ] Cascade phase: Derive_ComputedValue keeps percentages as-is (computed value = percentage)
- [ ] Layout phase: BoxModel.Resolve_Horizontal() resolves percentages against containing block
- [ ] Layout phase: BoxModel.Resolve_Vertical() resolves percentages against containing block
- [ ] Percentage resolvers should ONLY be called during layout (boxes guaranteed to exist)
- [ ] If box is null during layout, throw InvalidOperationException (indicates pipeline bug)
- [ ] Update tests to use ForceFullLayout() which runs complete pipeline in correct order
- [ ] Add integration tests verifying percentage resolution happens during layout, not cascade

#### 14.5.12 BoxModel.Resolve() Bugs (from BoxModelTests)
Bugs discovered by comprehensive BoxModel unit tests (29 tests: 14 passing, 15 failing).
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/visudet.html

**Auto Width Resolution:**
- [ ] Fix AsDecimal() called on AUTO values in Resolve_Horizontal() - throws exception
- [ ] Block with width: auto should fill containing block minus margins
- [ ] Inline-block with width: auto should shrink-to-fit (requires intrinsic sizing)

**Auto Margin Centering (CSS 2.2 §10.3.3):**
- [ ] Fix margin-left: auto + margin-right: auto centering returns 0 instead of calculated value
- [ ] Single auto margin (left or right) should absorb remaining horizontal space
- [ ] Verify auto margins work with explicit width

**Min/Max Constraints (CSS 2.2 §10.4, §10.7):**
- [ ] Fix min-width not clamping resolved width upward
- [ ] Fix max-width not clamping resolved width downward
- [ ] Fix min-height not clamping resolved height upward
- [ ] Fix max-height not clamping resolved height downward
- [ ] Apply constraints AFTER percentage/auto resolution

**Over-Constrained Horizontal (CSS 2.2 §10.3.3):**
- [ ] When width + margins + padding + border > containing block width
- [ ] LTR: margin-right becomes auto (absorbs overflow)
- [ ] RTL: margin-left becomes auto (absorbs overflow)

**Absolute Positioning Constraint Equation (CSS 2.2 §10.3.7):**
- [ ] Fix left: auto calculation (should position based on static position)
- [ ] Fix right: auto calculation
- [ ] Fix top: auto calculation
- [ ] Fix bottom: auto calculation
- [ ] Verify constraint equation: left + margin-left + border-left + padding-left + width + padding-right + border-right + margin-right + right = containing block width

**UpdateContentWidth() Crash:**
- [ ] Fix crash when width is still AUTO after resolution
- [ ] Ensure width is always resolved to a numeric value before accessing

